course: dictionary
lesson: 5126
title: The word invention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An invention is a new thing that someone has made or thought of for the first time. Invention can also mean the act of inventing something, as in «the invention of writing». A third meaning is a made-up story that is not true.
explain: «The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention which men will one day call writing.» Here invention means a new thing. The words «great» and «will one day call» show it is something new that will change how people live.
explain: An invention is often a new thing or a new way of doing something that solves a problem. Ask yourself: what problem does this invention solve? If you can answer, you have found the meaning.
fact: Invention is a noun: an invention, inventions.
fact: «An invention is a new thing or a new way of doing something that solves a problem.»
fact: Metal rivets on jeans were patented in 1873 to stop pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.
fact: Along the Silk Road travelled not only goods but also ideas, religions and inventions.
fact: «Necessity is the mother of invention» means people often invent new things when they really need them.
exercise: Which sentence best describes an invention? | An old thing that nobody uses any more | *A new thing or new way of doing something that solves a problem | A rule that stops people playing outside | A kind of weather
exercise: «The story about the dragon was an invention; it never really happened.» What does invention mean here? | A new kind of metal | A famous explorer | *A made-up story that is not true | The act of building a bridge
exercise: «Along the Silk Road travelled not only goods but also ideas, religions and inventions.» Which word means new things people made? | travelled | goods | *inventions | Silk
test: «The printing press was a great invention.» In this sentence, invention means: | A quiet place to sleep | A type of food | *A new thing that someone made | A long walk
test: The saying «necessity is the mother of invention» means: | Needing things makes you lazy | Only rich people make inventions | *People often invent new things when they really need them | Inventions are never useful
exam: «Getting used to an invention does not mean ignoring its real risks.» What does this teach us? | *Even when we get used to an invention, we should still notice its real risks | Inventions have no risks at all | Using a new invention is always safe, so never check the risks | You should accept every new invention without thinking
